<title>USA: Exporters sell 101,600 tonnes corn to Japan-USDA.</title>
<headline>Exporters sell 101,600 tonnes corn to Japan-USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Private exporters reported the sale of 101,600 tonnes of U.S. corn to Japan for delivery during the 1996/97 marketing year, Agriculture Department said Friday.</p>
<p>The marketing year began Sept 1 for corn.</p>
<p>By law, exporters are required to promptly report sales of more than 100,000 tonnes of grain.</p>
</text>
